pages.content:
Java programs use variables to store values of specific types. Common primitive types include `int`, `double`, `char`, and `boolean`. Variables can be initialized when declared, and operators can combine or compare values.

Example:
```java
int age = 21;
double price = 49.50;
char grade = 'A';
boolean active = true;
```

codeCard.code:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int age = 21;
        double price = 49.50;
        char grade = 'A';
        boolean active = true;
        System.out.println(age + " " + price + " " + grade + " " + active);
    }
}

